134	195	Life and career
Solbes was born in Pinoso on 31 August 1942.

195	357	While independent in the sense of not being affiliated to any party, his various ministerial roles in Spain were always within Socialist Workers' Party cabinets.

357	441	From 1985 to 1991, he was third 3rd secretary of state for the European Communities.
442	621	He was agriculture and fisheries minister (1991–1993) and finance minister (1993–1996) in Felipe González's cabinets, also MP representing Alicante for the same party until 1999.

621	868	Appointed by Spanish premier José María Aznar (of the main competing party, the People's Party), Solbes was a European commissioner for economic and monetary affairs in the European Commission preside
868	1032	Then Solbes served as second vice president and minister of economy and finance in the government of José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero, which he held from 2004 to 2009.

1032	1094	Solbes died from cancer on 18 March 2023, at the age of 80.



